cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this graph, please cite it as below."
title: "R(10,12) >= 857: an 856-vertex Ramsey graph"
version: "1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Chrisbacher
    given-names: Peter J.
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: "A graph on 856 vertices with no K10 and no independent set of size 12, improving the lower bound for the Ramsey number R(10,12) from 856 (Google Research, the best public bound we could find as of 24 November 2026) to 857. Built by Theorem 3 of Xu, Shao and Radziszowski (SIAM J. Discrete Math. 25 (2011)) from the Paley graph on 797 vertices and a 39-vertex block of Google Research's R(10,12) graph, with a larger 20-vertex common induced subgraph and a valid split, and checked by independently written exact programs."
keywords: [Ramsey numbers, lower bounds, graph construction]
